# No em dashes in frontend

Never use the em dash character (`—`) or en dash (`–`) anywhere in the marketing site / frontend (`client/**`).

## Use instead

- Comma: `Air, Sea, and Road`
- Colon: `Yes: FCL and LCL are supported.`
- Period (new sentence) when the clause stands alone
- Regular hyphen only for compound words (`real-time`, `gate-in`) or file/ID ranges when required (`JOB/FI/2026/00223`)

## Do not

- Do not use `—` in UI strings, meta descriptions, testimonials, comments, or CSS
- Do not “fix” with spaced hyphens as a stand-in for em dashes (`word - word`); prefer comma or colon
